WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.301
-Today is Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.603
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.006
You know, I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.874
and I, of course,
send out thank-you notes.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.043
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:13.079
-Wow.
-Feels good to hear applause.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.647
We haven't heard that in a year.
That's amazing.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.416
-Wow!
-Thank you, guys.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.985
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.620
I was running
a bit behind today.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.888
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.089
So I was getting --
-Why's that?

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.991
-Well, remember all those
tattoos I got removed?

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.292
-Yeah.
-I'm reapplying them.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.361
-Are you serious?
-Yeah, I second-guessed it.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.295
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.763
So I spent all day doing that.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.199
And I forgot to write out
my thank-you notes.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.535
So I was just wondering,
can I write it out right now?

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.870
Do you guys mind?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.405
I appreciate that.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:42.141
James, can I get some thank you
note writing music, please?

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:43.709
♪♪

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.211
-Okay.
-Wow.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.180
-He's just Zooming in.
That's not even James.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.049
-Wow.
-I think his picture froze.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:54.554
-He looks great.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.721
-You know it feels good
to be here for this.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:56.890
-What's that?
[ Music stops ]

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.558
[ Laughter ]
-I haven't been here all year.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.726
This is the first time
in a year I've seen you --

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:02.262
-Yeah, you were waiting,
and I was about to do it.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.130
-You guys are working.
I had to be at home,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.198
hanging out.
-Yep, I understood.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.299
-Goofing off.
-But then here it is.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.466
-But you guys held
the fort down, yeah.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:08.868
Glad it's here.
-Wow.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.402
-Just, thank you.
I love you.

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:12.505
I'm glad I'm here.
That's all.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.506
-All right, man.
You know what?

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:17.210
[ Applause ]

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.178
It's all about timing, you know?
-Yeah, it is.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.813
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.315
'Cause my heart, just --
You know what I mean?

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.083
It's, like --
It feels good to see you.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.752
It feels good to see The Roots.
Feels good to see an audience.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.820
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.489
-Go ahead.
I can't wait to hear these.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.623
-Feels good to see you.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.824
-Yeah, I can't wait
to hear these.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.492
-You can't wait, yeah.
It's about to happen.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.427
-Well, I love them. They're my
favorite part of the show.

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:37.863
-Yeah. Well, here it is,
right here for you.

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:38.965
♪♪
-I also love --

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.366
[ Laughter ]
-Many things --

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.634
There's many things
that we could do.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.870
-I love many things.
But go ahead, you go ahead.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.138
-I just want to
talk to the control room,

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.639
see if we can
turn your microphone off.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.240
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.475
They said yes.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:52.811
-[ Imitating mic cutting out ]
I --o --ove it.

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:56.549
-All right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.851
-My mic wasn't...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.220
-I was doing a bit.
I was doing a bit.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.622
I was doing a bit,
pretending my mic was cut.

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:05.124
'Cause, you know what
the most important thing --

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:08.094
This is the only -- This is
the last thing I'm gonna do.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:10.929
This is the lesson I learned
through all of this

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:13.499
whole horrible,
all of the stuff,

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.000
all the horrible things
were happening,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.870
the people --
the best to me.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.906
That's all.
-Your mic cut out.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:22.575
That was a beautiful thing
you just said.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.244
-Yeah, go ahead.
I'm good.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.180
-Oh, that was --
I wish we had the microphone on.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.650
-Oh, what's that?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.951
♪♪

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.520
-Thank you,
Biden's press conference,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.422
for feeling like going
to a Yanni concert

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.624
after four years
of listening to Slipknot.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.193
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:44.631
-Oh.
-I like Yanni.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.933
-Come on.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.368
♪♪

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:52.438
-Thank you, "Godzilla vs. Kong,"
for giving vaccinated couples

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.939
the ultimate reason to go out,

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:56.142
watching two hours of
a different couple fighting.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.379
[ Applause ]

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.314
"It's not us!"
-"Not us, baby."

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:04.917
-"It's not us.
That's all that matters."

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.252
♪♪

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:09.889
Thank you, giant ship
blocking the Suez Canal,

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.890
for causing flashbacks
for anyone that's had

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.093
to move a couch into
a New York City apartment.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.762
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.931
You know what I'm talking about.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:22.001
-My fingers.
-"What if we move it this way?"

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:25.972
-"Flip it like an L!
Flip it like an L!"

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.740
♪♪

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.711
-Thank you,
Pepsi's new Peeps-flavored soda,

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.646
for turning "Is Pepsi okay?"

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.415
into, "No, seriously,
is Pepsi, like, okay?"

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:40.119
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.556
-Mmm.
Yellow can.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.557
-Did you get that?
-I got it.

00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:47.660
-What'd you think?
Okay.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.561
-Eh...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:51.030
-Never mind.
-Eh...

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.898
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:56.669
-They can't all be winners.
You know what I mean?

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.271
-You talking about the jokes
or the soda?

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.739
-Everything.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.273
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:02.341
If everybody's a winner --

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.609
Somebody's gotta
watch the parade.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.411
That's all I'm saying.
You know what I mean?

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.746
Every joke can't be a winner.
Every soda can't be a winner.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:11.283
Go ahead.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:13.219
-That joke was pretty good.
-Yeah, I loved it.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.353
-Is it your favorite?
-I'm just saying,

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.789
as a general note,
all things can't win.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.458
Somebody's got to be number two.
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.059
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.427
-Why would you point to me
when you said "number two"?

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:25.998
-No reason.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:27.934
-I don't want
to point any fingers, but, uh...

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.468
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.404
-You have three pointing
back at you.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.973
-Every finger's pointing at me.
-You have 10 fingers?

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.374
-Wow.
-Two thumbs.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.610
-Two thumbs.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.877
♪♪

00:04:38.877 --> 00:04:42.314
-Thank you, Joe Biden supporting
universal pre-k,

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:43.950
although I'm pretty sure
it's just so that

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.550
you'll have somewhere
to leave Pete Buttiegieg

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:47.120
between 9:00 and 3:00.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.255
[ Applause ]

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.257
He's young.
-He's just a young man.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.192
-He's a young man.
-He's a young man.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.561
-Don't judge.
-Come on.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.929
♪♪

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.865
Thank you, spring,
for introducing us all

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:02.801
to the fun new game,
allergies or COVID?

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.437
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.639
-"That's it -- I got it!"
-"I got COVID.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:10.242
What do I do?"
-"Scratchy throat, yes."

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:11.911
-Don't go to WebMD!

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:16.449
Oh, my gosh, I'm gonna die.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.984
♪♪

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:21.387
Thank you, spring cleaning.
I can't wait to clean my house

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.190
and wipe down every surface
after spending a full year

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.392
cleaning my house
and wiping down every surface.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:31.097
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.465
Oh, dude, you can do
your best impression.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.300
-Oh, yeah.
[ Imitating spray bottle ]

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.601
-A Windex bottle.
-Ready? Do it.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.669
-Ready?

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.637
-[ Imitating spray bottle ]

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:41.373
[ Imitating window squeaking ]

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:43.542
[ Imitating spray bottle ]

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.244
[ Imitating window squeaking ]

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.279
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:49.881
[ Imitating birds chirping ]

00:05:49.881 --> 00:05:51.583
[ Imitating gunshot ]

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:53.319
[ Imitating bird falling ]

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.120
Pbht!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.523
[ Laughter ]
-Man...

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.124
-It's been a while.
-Yeah, well...

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:00.359
-Steve Higgins, everybody.
-It's been a while!

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.128
Come on!
We're back!

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:04.463
-For your consideration,
Emmy voters.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.032
[ Laughter ]
Right?

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:08.967
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:11.137
-Any voters.
-Any voters.

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:12.572
♪♪

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:16.075
Thank you, firing up the grill
the first time this season,

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:19.178
for reminding me that I meant to
clean the grill last September.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:19.945
[ Applause ]

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:22.781
"Eh, it'll burn off."

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:24.883
"That makes it taste better."

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:27.185
-"You need the grill,
you need the soot,

00:06:27.185 --> 00:06:28.287
you need the grease."

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.688
-"That makes the burger
taste better."

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:32.124
-"Without it,
it's just propane."

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:35.061
-"That's like eating --
I'd rather eat nothing."

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.429
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:38.798
"I'd rather starve myself."
-"I'd rather starve myself

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.232
than eat off a --
A guy who eats off

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:42.567
a clean grill --"
-"Is a real idiot."

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.103
-"Yeah.
Is no good in my book.

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:46.239
Might as well kick him
in the cojones."

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.007
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.476
-"That's what I would do.
If someone tried to cook me

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.645
a clean burger
on a clean grill..."

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:54.213
-"Right."
-"I'd kick that person

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.314
in the cojones."

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.883
-"It's the only logical thing
to do!"

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:58.817
-"Exactly."
-"You got logic on your side.

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:00.018
You got mathematics,
you got logic,

00:07:00.018 --> 00:07:01.420
you got everything on your side

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.621
telling you
you're in the right."

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:04.290
-"I'm so happy
you're my neighbor."

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:08.928
-"Me too!
I'm so glad we live in this --

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:12.130
in this shipping container
in the back of the Walmart.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.900
I love it."
-I think it's --

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.736
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:19.104
-It's been a year!
Come on, man.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:22.475
Little rusty.
-Little rusty.

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.877
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.278
♪♪

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:30.282
-Thank you, matzah, or as I call
you, swole saltines.

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:32.718
There you have it, everybody!
Those are my thank-you notes!

